# GenGrowth production provider handoff template
#
# 1. Copy this file to `.env.gengrowth-production.local`.
# 2. Choose exactly ONE provider block below and fill only that block in the
#    local copy. Do not use a ChatGPT/Codex login or browser cookie as a key.
# 3. Save the file. Tell Codex “已填好配置文件” — do not paste the key in chat.
# 4. Codex will validate the file locally without printing secret values, then
#    apply the minimal required variables to Railway production Worker and
#    Vercel production Web.
#
# The `.local` filename is ignored by Git. This template contains no secrets
# and is safe to keep in the repository.

# =========================
# Railway: production Worker — choose one provider
# =========================
# Required for both providers: use the literal provider name below.
LLM_PROVIDER=openai

# ---------- Option A: Direct OpenAI ----------
# Required only for Direct OpenAI: paste a newly-created API Platform
# service-account key here. Do not add quotes, spaces, line breaks, or escaped
# `\\n` characters.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol
# Optional sampling temperature. The default is 0.2; Azure GPT-5.6 deployments
# currently require the default-compatible value 1.
OPENAI_TEMPERATURE=0.2

# ---------- Option B: Azure OpenAI ----------
# Required only for Azure: set ALL four values. The deployment is the name you
# chose in Azure AI Foundry (it may differ from the underlying model ID).
# Use the resource ROOT here; do not append `/openai/v1`, because this Worker
# builds the deployment-specific `/openai/deployments/...` request path itself.
# The API version is Azure's API contract version, not the model release date.
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://YOUR-RESOURCE-NAME.openai.azure.com
AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=
OPENAI_API_VERSION=2025-04-01-preview

# If you select Direct OpenAI, Codex will delete all four Azure variables from
# Railway. If you select Azure OpenAI, Codex will remove the unused Direct
# OpenAI key from Railway. Never leave a complete configuration for both.

# =======================================
# Vercel: production Web (no LLM secrets)
# =======================================
# The Web application submits persistent jobs only. It must never receive an
# OpenAI or Azure provider credential. No Vercel environment variables are
# needed for this provider switch.
#
# Codex will therefore make no LLM-secret change in Vercel; it will only
# verify that these secret names are absent from the production Web project.
